# minimum required Qore version
%requires qore >= 1.14.1
# assume local scope for variables, do not use "$" signs
%modern
# require type definitions everywhere
# strict argument handling
# enable all warnings

%requires(reexport) DataProvider
%requires FileLocationHandler
%requires(reexport) HttpClientIo

module HttpClientDataProvider {
    version = "1.2";
    desc = "user module providing a data provider API for HTTP servers";
    author = "David Nichols <david@qore.org>";
    url = "http://qore.org";
    license = "MIT";
    init = sub () {
        # register the data provider factory
        DataProvider::registerFactory(new HttpClientDataProviderFactory());
    };
}

/** @mainpage HttpClientDataProvider Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section httpclientdataproviderintro Introduction to the HttpClientDataProvider Module

    The %HttpClientDataProvider module provides a data provider API for HTTP servers through the
    @ref dataproviderintro "DataProvider" API.

    The following classes are provided by this module:
    - @ref HttpClientDataProvider::HttpClientCallDataProvider "HttpClientCallDataProvider"
    - @ref HttpClientDataProvider::HttpClientCallRequestDataType "HttpClientCallRequestDataType"
    - @ref HttpClientDataProvider::HttpClientCallResponseDataType "HttpClientCallResponseDataType"
    - @ref HttpClientDataProvider::HttpClientCallWithMethodRequestDataType "HttpClientCallWithMethodRequestDataType"
    - @ref HttpClientDataProvider::HttpClientCallWithoutBodyRequestDataType "HttpClientCallWithoutBodyRequestDataType"
    - @ref HttpClientDataProvider::HttpClientDataProviderFactory "HttpClientDataProviderFactory"
    - @ref HttpClientDataProvider::HttpClientDataProvider "HttpClientDataProvider"
    - @ref HttpClientDataProvider::HttpClientDataProviderBase "HttpClientDataProviderBase"
    - @ref HttpClientDataProvider::HttpClientDeleteDataProvider "HttpClientDeleteDataProvider"
    - @ref HttpClientDataProvider::HttpClientGetDataProvider "HttpClientGetDataProvider"
    - @ref HttpClientDataProvider::HttpClientHeadDataProvider "HttpClientHeadDataProvider"
    - @ref HttpClientDataProvider::HttpClientOptionsDataProvider "HttpClientOptionsDataProvider"
    - @ref HttpClientDataProvider::HttpClientPatchDataProvider "HttpClientPatchDataProvider"
    - @ref HttpClientDataProvider::HttpClientPostDataProvider "HttpClientPostDataProvider"
    - @ref HttpClientDataProvider::HttpClientPutDataProvider "HttpClientPutDataProvider"

    @section httpclientdataprovider_client HTTP Requests

    Requests are made with a
    <a href="../../HttpClientIo/html/index.html">HttpClientIo::HttpClientConnectionManager</a>, which supports
    HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2, and HTTP/3; each data provider is created in one of the following ways:
    - from constructor options: a new connection manager is created from the transport options (timeouts,
      \c http_version, redirects, proxy, TLS verification, and the client certificate and key)
    - from a connection manager and a URL: the connection manager can be shared with other objects, and it is never
      closed by the data provider; see
      @ref HttpClientDataProvider::HttpClientDataProviderBase "HttpClientDataProviderBase"
    - from a synchronous @ref Qore::HTTPClient "HTTPClient": a new connection manager is created from the client's
      configuration, and the client itself is not used for requests

    The following settings of a synchronous @ref Qore::HTTPClient "HTTPClient" are carried over:
    |!Setting|!Carried over as
    |URL, including user information and the username and password options|the target URL; the credentials are sent with HTTP basic authentication
    |timeout and connect timeout|the request and connect timeouts of the connection manager
    |HTTP version|the protocol of the connection manager (\c "1.0" and \c "1.1" select HTTP/1.1)
    |maximum redirects and redirect passthrough|the redirect handling of the connection manager
    |proxy URL|the proxy of the connection manager
    |server certificate verification, client certificate and private key|the TLS settings of the connection manager
    |maximum response body size|the response body limit of the connection manager
    |default headers set in the constructor or with \c addDefaultHeaders()|default request headers
    |error passthrough and pre-encoded URLs|request options of the data provider
    |assumed encoding|the \c assume_encoding option

    Other settings, such as persistent connections, the connection path, and event queues,
    are not carried over.  The child data providers created by a data provider share its connection manager.

    Text responses without a \c charset are decoded as ISO-8859-1, the default character set of text media types in
    HTTP/1.1 (RFC 2616), as with @ref Qore::HTTPClient "HTTPClient", unless the \c assume_encoding option is set.
    A request body is sent with \c "Content-Type: application/octet-stream" (binary data) or \c "text/plain" with
    the string's character encoding, unless a \c Content-Type header is given.

    Responses keep the format of @ref HttpClientDataProvider::HttpClientCallResponseDataType
    "HttpClientCallResponseDataType", and errors are raised with the codes of the synchronous client: an error status
    raises \c HTTP-CLIENT-RECEIVE-ERROR (unless the \c error_passthru option is set), a timeout raises
    \c SOCKET-TIMEOUT, and redirect errors raise \c HTTP-CLIENT-MAXIMUM-REDIRECTS-EXCEEDED or
    \c HTTP-CLIENT-REDIRECT-ERROR.  Request paths are percent-encoded like the synchronous client encodes them,
    unless the \c pre_encoded_urls option is set.

    @section httpclientdataprovider_relnotes Release Notes

    @subsection httpclientdataprovider_v1_2 HttpClientDataProvider v1.2
    - requests are made with a
      <a href="../../HttpClientIo/html/index.html">HttpClientIo::HttpClientConnectionManager</a> instead of a
      synchronous @ref Qore::HTTPClient "HTTPClient"; a synchronous client passed to a data provider is
      converted, see @ref httpclientdataprovider_client
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/5469">issue 5469</a>)
    - added the @ref HttpClientDataProvider::HttpClientDataProviderBase "HttpClientDataProviderBase" class and
      constructors taking a connection manager and a URL
    - the public \c http member of the data providers is only set if the data provider was created from an
      @ref Qore::HTTPClient "HTTPClient"
    - fixed the \c ssl_cert_location and \c ssl_key_location options with a location URL, which were used as file
      paths
    - option default values are applied

    @subsection httpclientdataprovider_v1_1 HttpClientDataProvider v1.1
    - added the \c headers option to allow auth headers to be set in the data provider
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4695">issue 4695</a>)

    @subsection httpclientdataprovider_v1_0_1 HttpClientDataProvider v1.0.1
    - added support for the \c pre_encoded_urls option
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/4656">issue 4656</a>)

    @subsection httpclientdataprovider_v1_0 HttpClientDataProvider v1.0
    - initial release of the module
*/

#! contains all public definitions in the HttpClientDataProvider module
public namespace HttpClientDataProvider {
}
